<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech chemical maker MCHZ 1996 net profit dips.</title>
<headline>Czech chemical maker MCHZ 1996 net profit dips.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech chemical maker Moravske Chemicke Zavody a.s. (MCHZ) said on Monday its audited net profit in 1996 dipped to 113 million crowns from 129 million in the previous year.</p>
<p>Results for year ending December 31, 1996 (in millions of crowns) :</p>
<p> Net profit		113.38    vs	129.37</p>
<p> Gross profit	    150.09    vs	257.06</p>
<p> Operating profit	217.51    vs	315.04</p>
<p>Sales of own goods</p>
<p> and services	  2,656.04    vs    2,935.84</p>
<p> Total assets	  3,966.13    vs    3,171.65</p>
<p> Basic capital	 1,721.03    vs    1,721.03</p>
<p>Note - Full company name is Moravske Chemicke Zavody as. MCHZ shares are traded on the main market of the Prague Stock Exchange. Czech chemicals, arms and communications conglomerate Chemapol Group holds a 60 percent stake in the company.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
